summary: Verify tang_pub in /rec response and binding storage semantics
description: |
    Verify the /rec/$kid endpoint returns tang_pub in its response, that the
    returned key is correct and public-only, and that ECMR recovery semantics
    are preserved. Also verify that new and regenerated bindings omit stored
    Tang public keys (asserted on the JWE from LUKS2 token metadata), that
    legacy-format bindings with a stored advertisement are migrated by
    clevis luks regen, and that a tampered tang_pub returned in-flight is
    never used by clevis decrypt (failing closed when no /adv fallback is
    available).

    The test skips with a clear message when the tang build does not return
    tang_pub in /rec responses: it requires a tang build with tang_pub
    support, so run it against PQC-capable hosts only (tag: tang-pub).

    Phases:
    1. /rec/$kid includes tang_pub — public-only, matches ECMR identifier
    2. New bindings do not persist the Tang advertisement and unlock
    3. Legacy-format binding (stored advertisement) is migrated by regen
       and unlocks afterwards
    4. Mismatched tang_pub is discarded by clevis; decrypt fails closed
       when /adv is unavailable
component:
  - tang
  - clevis
  - jose
test: ./runtest.sh
require:
  - clevis
  - clevis-luks
  - cryptsetup
  - tang
  - jose
  - socat
  - curl
  - jq
  - python3
  - psmisc
  - util-linux
duration: 15m
enabled: true
tag:
  - pqc
  - tang-pub
  - Tier2
tier: '2'
extra-summary: /CoreOS/clevis/Sanity/tang-pub-binding
extra-task: /CoreOS/clevis/Sanity/tang-pub-binding
adjust:
  - enabled: false
    when: distro < rhel-10
    continue: false
  - enabled: false
    when: distro < fedora-45
    continue: false
